CHARACTER=A cheerful young beaver carpenter: warm chestnut-brown fur, a cream muzzle with two big white front teeth showing under a dark-brown nose, small round ears, and a broad flat dark-brown paddle tail. A turquoise knitted long-sleeved sweater with a ribbed collar and ribbed cuffs, mustard-yellow trousers held by a brown belt with a gold buckle, and red boots. Dark-brown mitten paws. Both paws are empty: no tools or props.
PIECES=Row 1: head base (the furry chestnut-brown beaver head with its cream muzzle, the two white front teeth and the dark-brown nose, plain fur forehead and eye areas), left ear, right ear (small round brown ears). Row 2: torso (the turquoise sweater with its ribbed collar, continuing up into a short brown fur neck and ending at the bottom of the sweater just above the belt; both shoulders are rounded turquoise sweater, and the sweater sides are painted down to the waist; no belt, trousers or legs on it), hips (the brown belt with its gold buckle and the top of the mustard-yellow trousers below it down to the crotch, painted whole, with two rounded leg openings), tail (the broad flat dark-brown paddle tail, with a rounded root). Row 3: four separate sleeve pieces, each painted upright: left upper arm, right upper arm (the upper half of the turquoise sleeve only, from shoulder to elbow, rounded at both ends, no cuff), left forearm, right forearm (the lower half of the turquoise sleeve only, from elbow to wrist, rounded at the top, with the ribbed cuff at the bottom); then left paw, right paw (dark-brown mitten paws, open and relaxed, rounded at the wrist). Row 4: left leg, right leg (one mustard-yellow trouser leg each, from the crotch down to its hem, rounded at the top, with nothing below the hem), left boot, right boot (red boots, rounded at the top).
HANDS=relaxed (exactly the paw of image_1, open and relaxed); open (palm facing the viewer, all fingers spread wide, as in a wave); fist (fingers curled into a soft round fist); point (index finger stretched straight down, the other fingers curled); thumbs-up (fingers curled into a fist, thumb sticking straight out sideways, away from the body); grip (fingers curled loosely forward and the thumb pressed against the side of the first finger, as when pinching something thin).
POSES=Row 1: left upper arm, left upper arm raised, right upper arm, right upper arm raised. An upper arm is only the turquoise sleeve from the shoulder down to the elbow, rounded at both ends, without any cuff (the ribbed cuff belongs to the forearm). A raised upper arm is the same sleeve at the same size and width as it looks on an arm lifted high above the head, but painted upright like the first one, shoulder end at the top: its shoulder end is a soft, slightly wider rounded cap with one or two gentle folds where the cloth bunches. Row 2: left boot, left boot on tiptoe, right boot, right boot on tiptoe (red boots; on tiptoe the boot is seen from the front with its toe pointing down and its sole tilted towards the viewer, as when jumping, with its rounded ankle end still at the top). Row 3: tail, then tail up (the broad flat dark-brown paddle tail; tail up is the same tail swung up and tilted, as when the beaver hops happily; both tails have their rounded root at the lower left, where they join the hips).
SLEEVES=Row 1: left whole sleeve, then right whole sleeve. A whole sleeve is the turquoise knitted sweater sleeve as ONE piece from the shoulder all the way down to the end of its ribbed cuff, painted straight and upright with the shoulder end at the top, the same width as image_1's sleeve along its whole length, with one soft fold at the elbow and the ribbed cuff at the bottom, and no paw. The right whole sleeve is the same sleeve for the other arm.
FIST=fist, palm side facing the viewer: the curled fingers and the thumb across them visible, wrist up, chunky dark-brown mitten paw like image_1.
LOWER=Row 1: hips (only the top of the mustard-yellow trousers: the brown belt with its gold buckle and the trousers below it down to the crotch and no further, painted whole, with two rounded leg openings just below the crotch; no trouser legs on it). Row 2: left leg, right leg (one mustard-yellow trouser leg each, from the crotch down to its rolled cuff at the hem, exactly as long and as wide as in image_1, rounded at the top, with nothing below the cuff). Row 3: tail (the broad flat dark-brown paddle tail exactly as it hangs in image_1: its narrow rounded root at the upper right, where it joins the hips, and the wide paddle at the lower left).
TAIL=Row 1: tail (the broad flat dark-brown paddle tail exactly as it hangs in image_1, at the same size: its narrow rounded root at the upper right, where it joins the hips behind the trousers, and the wide rounded paddle at the lower left, with the soft criss-cross pattern of image_1).
